# React & Next.js Patterns

## Server vs client

```tsx
// ✅ Server page — default
export default function SourcesPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <PageHero eyebrow="Credibility" title="Source Library" description="..." />
      <Container className="py-12 md:py-16">{/* content */}</Container>
    </>
  );
}

// ✅ Client only when needed (motion, hooks, browser APIs)
"use client";
export function AnimatedCounter() { /* ... */ }
```

## Page layout

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hero inside Container, inconsistent spacing
<Container className="py-16">
  <h1>Title</h1>
</Container>

// ✅ GOOD — full-bleed hero, contained body
<PageHero eyebrow="..." title="..." description="..." />
<Container className="py-12 md:py-16">{children}</Container>
```

## Styling

- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes.
- Prefer semantic tokens: `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-accent`.
- Tabler icons: `stroke={1.5}`, `aria-hidden` on decorative icons.

## Content

- Import sector/timeline/source data from `@/content/*` or `@/lib/content`.
- Never duplicate comparator metric formatting; use `@/lib/comparator-format`.
